     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The amount of interest, <i>I</i>, to be paid for one period of a loan with remaining principal, <i>P</i>, is <span data-math=\"I = P \\times \\frac{r}{n}\"></span>, where <i>r</i> is the interest rate in decimal form and <i>n</i> is the number of payments in a year. Because <i>r</i> is the interest rate in a year, <i>t</i> is 1 and does not impact the calculation. Note, interest paid to lenders is always rounded up to the nearest penny.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"I = 25,850 \\times \\frac{{0.029}}{{12}} = \\$62.48\"></span></p>\n"
